"""Reading comprehension, Year 7 (keys RD7.xx).

Twelve original passages, each written by hand for this bank, 350-550 words, seven questions each.
KS3 English reading (Year 7): inference backed by evidence, language and its effect (simile, metaphor,
personification, word choice), structure (how an opening sets things up, shifts in focus, how an ending
links back), the writer's viewpoint and purpose, fact and opinion, bias, and comparison within a text.

* RD7.01 a first day at secondary school (story)
* RD7.02 how vaccines work (explanation)
* RD7.03 a storm at sea (poem)
* RD7.04 the history of the printing press (information)
* RD7.05 a mountain rescue (story)
* RD7.06 Isambard Kingdom Brunel (biography)
* RD7.07 a family bakery (story)
* RD7.08 plastic in the oceans (speech)
* RD7.09 sleep and the teenage brain (explanation)
* RD7.10 a chess tournament (story)
* RD7.11 Samarkand and the Silk Road (travel writing)
* RD7.12 the Natural History Museum, London (review)

Non-fiction uses only well-established facts taught in English schools. To be reviewed line by line by a
second reader (an English teacher or the bank's reviewer) before release.
"""

